module gunbc.integration_concern.h11ssl_unit3_empty_census_lists_still_read_as_measured_nothing

// One row of the integration-concern register. The roster derives the row from this file (module gunbc.integration_concern.roster);
// there is no list to append to. Ported from main's block in gunbc.integration_concern
// at this merge.

import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { climbs_when }
import gunbc.integration_concern { CitesDeclaration, ConcernSighting, ExistingHome, IntegrationConcern, PreservedObligation, RequirementEstablished, SuspectedCapabilityGap, Triaged, h11ssl_unit3_build_pool_fork_sighting_revision, h11ssl_unit3_census_standing_sighting_revision }

// AN UNCENSUSED HOST IS NOW FENCED WHERE WIDTH IS ADMITTED, AND STILL READS AS MEASURED-NOTHING ELSEWHERE.
// Recorded rather than remembered: this PR fences the width path, and the folds themselves stay shaped as they are.
data h11ssl_unit3_empty_census_lists_still_read_as_measured_nothing: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "h11ssl_unit3_empty_census_lists_still_read_as_measured_nothing",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "compute_host_cpu_threads"),
    requirement: "a ComputeHost whose hardware lists are EMPTY states that the fleet has NOT read that axis, and no fold turns that emptiness into a measurement of nothing. THE STANDING NOW EXISTS, PER AXIS: gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent::host_hardware_census_of answers processors and memory as ProcessorAxis | MemoryAxis (each Surveyed { rows } or Unread, asked once by processor_axis / memory_axis); the disk axis joins with its consumer, since no fold reads a ComputeHost's storage list today (gunbc.design_argument::consumption), and the four reads derive their refusal from their OWN axis rather than testing emptiness as their own sibling leaf (gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization) -- compute_host_cpu_threads answers CpuThreadsCensusUnread and exposes the fold as processor_rows_thread_total so the width axis reads the axis once, compute_host_ram_bytes_total answers HostRamCensusUnread, compute_host_primary_cpu answers PrimaryCpuCensusUnread so a refusal says no census was read instead of claiming the machine has no CPU, and compute_host_cpu_admitted_width's OWN empty-list check is replaced by the standing rather than kept beside it. Controls: test.claim.fleet.fleet_intent_memory_witness::unsurveyed_census_refuses_the_host_ram_read, ::unsurveyed_census_refuses_threads_and_primary_cpu, ::mtcollins1_memory_axis_is_unread_and_its_ram_read_refuses, ::srv1_memory_axis_is_surveyed_and_answers_a_measured_total, and test.claim.runner.runner_slot_allocation_witness::an_offer_with_no_processor_census_refuses_the_cores_axis_rather_than_measuring_zero_cores. gunbc.host.host_effect_realize::provision_build_cache_arch_unknown_host_fixture still builds the same shape on purpose -- a host known by identity whose processor inventory is empty, the shape a freshly-racked srvN has before its read lands -- and its claim is still that realization must REFUSE it. WHAT THIS SHAPE CANNOT YET SAY is \"the axis WAS read and it really holds nothing\": an empty list reads as Unread for every axis, so a host whose memory had been surveyed and found absent would need the axis standing DECLARED on the row rather than derived from its list; no host in this corpus makes that claim, so the shape is not stretched to cover one. WHAT THE STANDING DOES NOT CARRY is the READ: this unit's axes are unread, and a census-less offer sits in gunbc.ci.ci_fleet::fleet_owned_compute_offer_catalog only because every consumer of those four reads now refuses for the right reason",
    standing: RequirementEstablished {
      by: CitesDeclaration {
        declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.state_space_conflation", decl_name: "state_space_conflation"),
      },
    },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "host_hardware_census_of"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "memory_axis"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "processor_rows_thread_total"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "compute_host_cpu_threads"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "compute_host_ram_bytes_total"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "compute_host_primary_cpu"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_allocation", decl_name: "compute_host_cpu_admitted_width"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_runner_placement", decl_name: "host_deployment_standing_given"),
    ],
  },
  question: "Who takes the READ that puts rows in this unit's axes -- the in-band dmidecode -t processor / -t baseboard and the lsblk / sfdisk reads its intake rows name -- and turns each Unread axis into Surveyed? And is a census-less offer standing in gunbc.ci.ci_fleet::fleet_owned_compute_offer_catalog a fleet policy or a one-off: this PR admits it on the ruling of the responsible session (smart-crane-730, review exchange on PR #16602, 2026-11-18, quoted in that PR's body) because the four reads now refuse for the right reason; nobody has ruled for census-less offers in general.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: h11ssl_unit3_build_pool_fork_sighting_revision,
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration {
          declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.state_space_conflation", decl_name: "state_space_conflation"),
        },
        tail: [
          CitesDeclaration {
            declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.host_effect_realize", decl_name: "provision_build_cache_arch_unknown_host_fixture"),
          },
          CitesDeclaration {
            declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_allocation", decl_name: "compute_host_cpu_admitted_width"),
          },
        ],
      },
      account: "Sighted 2026-11-17 in review 96030, read against head 091f3a9b924ba4ff63268fee3f289d8ef14a27c6. This unit is the first offer in the corpus whose processors are listed EMPTY, so the fold's init: 0 became a live answer: its cores axis read AxisAdmits with slots 0 -- a machine measured at no cores -- and a comment, not the machinery, promised the refusal. That PR fenced the width path only: the cores axis became AxisUnmeasured and the width refuses with a cause that names the unit, while the folds stayed unfenced and any future consumer of them inherited the same zero.",
    },
    tail: [
      ConcernSighting {
        revision: h11ssl_unit3_census_standing_sighting_revision,
        evidence: FreeSemigroup {
          head: CitesDeclaration {
            declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "host_hardware_census_of"),
          },
          tail: [
            CitesDeclaration {
              declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.fleet.fleet_intent_memory_witness", decl_name: "unsurveyed_census_refuses_the_host_ram_read"),
            },
            CitesDeclaration {
              declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_argument", decl_name: "root_generalization"),
            },
          ],
        },
        account: "Re-read 2026-11-18 in review 96379, against head 6be8eaef58a481519c839f9ade82e2ae027554f7, which found the previous fence INCOMPLETE: only compute_host_cpu_admitted_width asked the census, so compute_host_cpu_threads still folded to hardware_thread_count(0), compute_host_ram_bytes_total still answered byte_size(0), and compute_host_primary_cpu's refusal sentence claimed the machine has no primary CPU rather than that nobody had read it. Recording that gap did not license it (gunbc.design_argument::continuous_generalization: recording neither satisfies an obligation nor authorizes a deviation) -- the review was right to call the catalog admission blocking. The first cut of the fix asked the question ONCE per host and answered Surveyed when ANY of the three lists had rows; re-read on 2026-11-18 that grain was itself wrong, and it made mtcollins1's empty memory list a MEASURED zero -- nobody read zero DIMMs on that board, its memory was never read -- so the standing is per axis (ProcessorAxis / MemoryAxis / StorageAxis) and each read refuses from its own axis. Consequence, stated rather than buried: mtcollins1_offer's RAM answer changes from a measured zero to HostRamCensusUnread, asserted in test.claim.runner.mtcollins1_runner_offer_witness::mtcollins1_RED_nominal_dram_total_reaches_neither_offer_nor_reader and in test.claim.fleet.fleet_intent_memory_witness::mtcollins1_memory_axis_is_unread_and_its_ram_read_refuses, with srv1 as the green half (::srv1_memory_axis_is_surveyed_and_answers_a_measured_total). The axis census of the catalog at that head: seven offers; srv1-srv4 and srv14 have all three axes populated; mtcollins1_runner_host has a read processor axis and unread memory and storage axes; supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_host has three unread axes and is the only offer whose processor reads newly refuse.",
      },
    ],
  },
  disposition: Triaged {
    home: ExistingHome { model: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "host_hardware_census_of") },
    preserve: [
      PreservedObligation {
        holder: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_allocation", decl_name: "compute_host_cpu_admitted_width"),
        control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_slot_allocation_witness", decl_name: "an_offer_with_no_processor_census_refuses_the_cores_axis_rather_than_measuring_zero_cores"),
        statement: "the width axis keeps refusing an unread census, and refuses it for the named host -- it does not re-derive the refusal from an empty list of its own",
      },
      PreservedObligation {
        holder: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent", decl_name: "compute_host_ram_bytes_total"),
        control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.fleet.fleet_intent_memory_witness", decl_name: "unsurveyed_census_refuses_the_host_ram_read"),
        statement: "an unread MEMORY AXIS reaching the RAM read answers HostRamCensusUnread, never byte_size(0) -- the axis grain is what makes mtcollins1 a refusal and srv1 a measurement",
      },
    ],
    next: climbs_when(capability: "a run takes the in-band census this unit's intake rows name (dmidecode -t processor and -t baseboard, lsblk and sfdisk) and admits it against this host, so each axis of gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent::host_hardware_census_of answers Surveyed with real rows and the offer's reads start measuring; and if a host ever needs \"read, and genuinely empty\", that is the moment the axis standing moves from derived to declared on the row"),
  },
}
